{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on request ab49145b, for S4: option A. A legacy mapping with an\nunknown owner stays as it is, and new consent on that binding is\nrefused.\n\n1. The `pending_op` column stands, with its three values: NULL for a\n   legacy row, an operation for a provisional owner, and the empty\n   string for a confirmed mapping.\n2. A legacy row is never confirmed. New consent that uses its binding\n   gets the existing 503 `temporarily_unavailable`. Access and refresh\n   admission for tokens that already exist do not change in this head.\n3. Option B is not built. Its fence must hold on every grant path for\n   every client of an Agent, and that is too much mechanism for rows\n   that have no future. Every live Worker answers 404 on /mcp today,\n   and the identifiers cutover retires each room that holds a legacy\n   row, with its registry.\n4. The note says how a person gets past the refusal before the cutover:\n   they make a new Agent. If that is wrong, tell me.\n5. Witness: a legacy row refuses new consent and stays NULL, and a new\n   mapping goes from provisional to confirmed.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}